## Notable implementation decisions (please sanity-check in review)
- **Blocks are `QGraphicsItem`s, not `QWidget`s.** The skill's example assumed
  `block.show()/grab()`. `compare_screenshot` was extended to render graphics
  items through a `QGraphicsScene` instead. (#2/#4)
- **Window title test relaxed.** Issue #3 asks `windowTitle() == "Silmulator"`,
  but the real title is `"Silmulator — SIL/HIL/CIL Hardware Simulator"`. The
  test asserts the **prefix** rather than changing the app's title (out of scope).
- **Multimeter render is non-deterministic** — it paints a reading with random
  Gaussian noise. The block test freezes `_get_reading` to a constant so its
  golden is reproducible. (#4)
- **Auto-placed blocks land off-screen.** The canvas test calls the app's own
  `fit_all()` so the PSU block is actually visible in the golden. (#5)
- **pytest config in `pyproject.toml`, not a new `pytest.ini`** — a `pytest.ini`
  would take precedence and silently drop the existing `testpaths`. (#2)
- **`.gitignore` paths anchored under `Silmulator/`** (the Python project is a
  subdirectory of the git root); also added `.venv`/pycache hygiene.

